      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>CORONATION,</head>
        <p>THE CORONATION,</p>
        <p>GREAT SANKEY.</p>
        <p>The General Committee appointed in June is now completing arrangements for toe enti7rtainment and sports postponed on ascount of the illness of his Majesty the Kin,. The date far the treat Co tlao old folks aid children has been fixed for Friday, August Bth, in the Sunday school, and the vicarig^ field, kindly lent by Rev J R Jones. There is un &amp;align with regard Co the refresninents, priz Sze. 'Dose will be supplied by the same trade,imen who sn v ry generously assisted the eonatnittee in holding the orders over. A gmeral meet- ing of the Ladies' and Gantlemen's 'iommittem sod helpers is to be bald not week to reoeive the final report 6f arrangements, details o! which are in the hands of 3dessrs T Halton, W Hodgkinson and Fulten Smith.</p>
