      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0062" n="art0062">
        <head>epties, et c</head>
        <p>epties, et c</p>
        <p>_B R WISE IN TIME AND FURNISH AT</p>
        <p>yours7i, "ta'risiVir.i ST E R (Just past Station, through Railway Arch). ALS* AT PITTS'S PANTHEON, GAYTHORN Oust past Manchester Central Station). PATRONISED By ROYALT.Y. NOBILITY.</p>
        <p>WHAT'S IN A NAME? That which we term a rose, If °idled lov coy other name would smell as sweet. Young and unsophisticated as she was, Juliet,never- theless,voiced a truism when she so expressed herself. Still despite this, there Is e Very considerable value, both senti- mental and financial in a good name, especially in these keen competitive and not, we regret to say over scrupulous times. Nowadays a good name is more precious then rubies —in fact, some firms would not part with their's for all the wealth in the world. A good name is not only a source of pride to its possessor, but a safeguard to the public. Take, for Instance, the name of PIT FS'S, which for many year, has been familiar in your mouths as a household word. This name In connection with an article hall-marks it as thoroughly reliable durable, tasteful, and the . best value obtainable Everyone of experience Is aware of this, hence the ever- Increasing volume of puniness flowing to PITT6'S of LON DON-ROAD and GAYTHORN.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S PEERLESS HOUSES OF FURNI- TURE at 15i, 22f, 28i, 38i, 50, 75, 100, 20), up to 1,000 guineas, are the embodiment of everything that is excell- ent and necessary for the embellishment of the home. They are incomparably superior in VALUE end appearance to others. They comprise articles of rarest beauty though thoroughly substantial, and can be had for ABOUT HALF expensive City prices. Full particulars and ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUlDll,containinz 700 artistic designs,priced post free. Cash quotations only. Easy payments ten per cent extra.</p>
        <p>PITTS'Ei SPECIAL, LIOUig OF FURNITURE, originally cost, we understand, about £5OO. PITTS'S price for the lot 200 guineas, or any article separately. It consists of TEN ROOMS, Hall, Stairs, Landings, artistically and substantially equipped. The late owner being wealthy. did not need to consider expenses. Briefly, the Rooms are as follows :—DRAWING ROOM, in Chippendale Mahogany and Rich Silk Tapestry ; DINING-ROOM, in Oak and Real Leather; MORNING-ROOM in Oriental Saddlebags; KITCHEN, SCULLERY, FIVE BEDROOMS, one each Walnut, Mahogany, Satin Walnut, Ash, and Decorated. All requisite number of articles, including Bedsteads, (two of which massive, all brass), carpets (Axminster. Brussels,&amp;c), rugs, mats, floor cloths, &amp;c., the whole forming an excep- tionally choice assemblage.</p>
        <p>PITT'S BEDSTEADS AND BEDDINCI.—Largest and best selection, being cleared out at giving-away prices. Rare chance for cheap lines</p>
        <p>pM'S CARPETS AND FuOOR COVERINGS.— A. Grand display. All British makes. Choicest designs, many of which exclusive: exquisitely blended colourings. Laid and Fitted free of charge.</p>
        <p>pars's RELIABLE CYCLES.—Splendid Selec- tion of over a Dozen Different High Grade Makes, RH fully guarantees. Any tyre fitted.</p>
        <p>DITT'S TRUNKS, TRAVELLING BAGS, Bassin- ettes, Mail Carta, Lamps, China, Glass, Bartbenware, Table Billiards. Bagatelle.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S POPULAR PlANOS.—Magnificent Die- play of NEW INSTRUMENTS by best makers, fully guaranteed, at Considerably Under Usual Prices. Also SIICOND-HAND PIANOs in good condition.</p>
        <p>pITTS'S OFFICE AND LIBRARY FURNI- TURN.—Bvery description of Bookcases. Secretalres Desks, ;stools, Chairs, Safes, Copying Presses, at about 11%1f City prices. Inspection will verify.</p>
