        <p>New Church Wanted at Burtonwood.</p>
        <p>Burtonwood is the parish with only one ecclesias- tical building—viz., a condemned church. Toe church building scheme is now being taken up warmly. A preliminary mewing was held on day, at at the Vicarage [louse. The Bishop of the diocese travelled from Liverpool to be present and to preside. Apologies for absence were received from Lord Lilford and the Archdeacon of Warring- ton. The Bishop, in the course of his remarks,said a new church was both necessary and desirable on the ground (al of structure, (b) of size, (c) of situation. The present building, his lordship remarked, has been condemned by the Ecclesiastical Commissioners ; and in his opinion it was the worst church in the diocese.—lts size is insufficient for present needs, and the space it affords 'or seating inadequate to the population of the parish. The present site is properly deemed unsatisfactory, being too far removed from the steadily increasing population of Collins Green. A resolution to this effect WM unanimously adopted. The Bishop believes that when the need of Button- wood becomes generally known, the diocese will be ready with help, and himself most generously promises a handsome contribution. :It was resolved to take immediate steps to secure a suitable and, if possible, free site for both church and hall, con- veniently placed with respec: both to Burtonwood and Collins Green—the chief centres of population. A first list of contributions will shortly be issued. A sum of £B,OOO at least will be required,</p>
        <p>FOOTBI,LL.</p>
        <p>NORI HERN RUGBY UNION. Lancashire County Union.</p>
        <p>The annual meeting of thia union was held at the Exchange Hotel, Manchester, on Tuesday. The report and balance- sheet were of a highly satisfactory character, the cash in hand being £253 8s 7d The following officers were elected : —President. R Walmsleygialford) ; secretary, J Platt (Old- barn); treasurer, 3 If Het:loton (rit Helens) ; committee, R Clo Hinge (Rochdale Hornets), J H Houghton (St Helens), El Ashton (Warrington), B Ashton (Werneth),l H Rills (Abbey J Parker (Barrow),J Wilkinson (Lancaster),J Reddish (Leigh), 3 Worthington (Swinton). 3 Ferguson (Morecambe), F Wright (Widnes), and F Hammerslay (Wigan).</p>
        <p>„ OEIRSHIRID COUNTY ('NION. The annual meeting of this union wits held under the presidency of Mr C Pownall (Runcorn). There wat a satis- factory balance in hand. The followino offi.Rals were elected : President. J Love (Birkenhead) ; vice-president, G Robinson (Runcorn) ; treasurer, 0 Pownall (Runcorn) ; secretary. J Love (Birkenhead); committee, J Welsh and 3 French (Stockport),P Harrison (Altrincham).and If Heith (Runcorn Reereation).r:The fixtures arranoed are :—October 25, v Lancashire at Runcorn • November 29. v Yorkshire in York- shire; and December 2, v Cumberland at Birkeuhead. The date for the Durham match is not, yet fixed. LANCASHIRE SENIOR CO)IPBTITION.</p>
        <p>A meeting for the purpose of disbanding this competition was held on Tuesday, Mr 3 Welsh (Stockport) presiding There is a sum of £l4O to be distributed. This it was agresd to divide between the various clubs for the purpose of paying subscriptions and entrance fee to the new league. The amount received by each club will be about £lO.</p>
