        <p>CIHLORODYNE is the best remedy known for a../ Coughs, Consumption, Bronchitis and Asthma. CLILORODYNE effectually checks and arrests those too often fatal diseases—Diphtheria, Fever, L'roup, Ague,. OHLORODYNE acts like a charm in Diarrhcea • and is the only specific in Cholera end Dysentery. CILORODYNE effectually cuts short all attacks of Epilepsy, Hysteria. Palpitation, and Spurns. frIILORODYNt is the only palliative in Neural- • gia, Rheumatism, Gout, Cancer, Toothache, Meningitis, Az. From Dr. B. J. BOIILTON AND CO., Horncastie. We have made pretty extensive use of Chlorodyne in our practice lately and look upon it as an excellent direct Seda- tive and Anti-spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion In whatever organ, and from whAteyer cause. It induces a feeling cf comfort and quietude rot obtainable by any other remedy, and it seems to posses this great advantage over all other sedatives ; that it leaves no unpleasant after effects. •• Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatch from her Majesty's Consul at Manilla to the effect that Cholera had been raging fearfully, and that the ONLY remedy of any service was CirILORO- DYNE."—See Lancet, Ist December. 1864.</p>
