        <p>Lancashire v Yorkshire. County Championship. This match in the County Championship was played at the Wigan Corperation Baths on Wednesday evening. beforo a crowded audience. The teams were as fol- lows :—Lancashire : Robertson (Warrington). goal : P Keatslev (Wigan) and Coe (Osborne), full backs ; T Saunders (Wigan), laalf back; F V Swift (Wigan). Lomax (S". Helens) and Crilfiilan (Burnley), for- wards. Yorkshire : Hartley (Halifax Park), goal : Clegg (Halifax) and Stocks (Halifax Park), full hacks Berry (Bradford), half-back; Anderson (Morley). Ridsdale (Bar,ey), and Ormondroyd (Bradford) forwards. Yorkshire defended the deep end in the first half, and early on they were called upon to defend their goal frcrn a combined attack by the Lancashire forwards. Gilfillan soon opened the scoring, while Saunders added a second goal immediately afterwards with a grand shot. Keeping up the pressure, Lancashire were soon three goals in front, Swift being the Scorer of the third. Yorkshire were completely out played, and further goals wera scored in quick suc- cession by Swift, Coe and Lomax (2). Half-time score : Lancashire 7 goals, Yorkshire nil. On resuming, York- shire played somewhat better, and the County Palatine citadel was endangered, Robertson being lucky to save. Saunders, however, removed play to the other end, and scored with a beautiful shot. This goal was quickly followed by two more from Lomax. Yorkshire thee pressed, and Robertson, after saving a couple of shots, was beaten by Ridsdale and Ormondroyd. Result : Lancashire 10 goals, Yorkshire 2 goals. Another Defeat for Warrington. The:St. Helens enthusiasts: mustered in strong ' force at the boundary-road Baths on Tuesday night, where the Liverpool League championship match, Warrington and St. Helens, was decided as well as the contest between St. Helens 2nd and Woolton Ist.gn both encounters the home swimmers woo easily. Woolton were only able to secure I goal against :6 put on by the St. Helens lade. In the League match Warrington were somewhat handi- capped. Sharrock and the St. Helens men easily' held the upper hand. Sharrock scored 3 goals, and Smith and Burrows 1 goal each. Ince scored twice- for Warriugton. Final :—St. Helens, 5 goals ; War- rington, 2 goals. CADBURY'S Cocos 'enure refined beverage. nutrition stimulating, ar d digestible. The" Lancet" says It" repie— sante the standard of highest purity." Entirely free from admixtures, such as kola, malt, hops alkali, etc. Insist upon having CADBURYS, as other hops, are sometimes übstituted for extra profit. In Packets and Tine only. (4.) ELASTIC STOCKINGS, KNEE CAPS, &amp;C.—For Varicose Vein' and all cases of Weakness and Swelling of the Legs, bprains &amp;c.; they are porous, light in texture, and Inexpensive an 4 are drawn on like an ordinary stocking. —Prices 4s 6d, 7s. 64 and 10s 6d each. Postage free.—WHITE AND WRIGHT, Sur- gioal Instrument and Truss Makers, 98, Renshaw-street .toP of Bold-street, Liverpool. - - TaIT. _ _ • ARGB STOOK OF MANDOLINES, isAicaoritt.4 11 GUITARS, VIOLINS, C. Special Offer.—Guaranteo !TAMAN MANDOLINE, MAKER'S name inside, Roar wood. ornamented: 10s. Si. Carriage paid. Best qoaiitl MOUTH ORGAN. Velvet lined Case le. post free. ARCHER AND SONS. STA '3 BORGES' CRESCENT. TOP OF LORD•STREET. nPooL. Established jos •</p>
